<lesson id="les-l7-02-two-cuts" title="Survive two cuts" level="7" minutes="15" goal="After the roadworks cut, no second cut strands a district"/>
<step n="1" text="Roadworks already tore the fibre between KecamatanSelatan and KecamatanBarat, so the ring is a line: Barat, Utara, Timur, Selatan. Ping LayananKota from WargaBarat: it still works, the long way through KecamatanUtara."/>
<step n="2" text="Trace one more break anywhere on the line: whoever sits past it is stranded. Each check below tries such a second cut."/>
<step n="3" text="Run a new fibre between KecamatanBarat GigabitEthernet0/1 and KecamatanSelatan GigabitEthernet0/2. Both ports already carry addresses in 10.70.3.0, so the routers pick the path up on their own." check="c1"/>
<step n="4" text="With the ring closed again, a break on either side of KecamatanSelatan must leave everyone reachable." check="c2"/>
<step n="5" text="And a break between KecamatanUtara and KecamatanTimur must not strand the south either." check="c3"/>
<check id="c1" kind="outage" from="pc1" to="server0" url="barat:GigabitEthernet0/2" expect="ok" label="WargaBarat still reaches LayananKota with the Barat to Utara fibre cut"/>
<check id="c2" kind="outage" from="pc0" to="server0" url="timur:GigabitEthernet0/2" expect="ok" label="WargaSelatan still reaches LayananKota with the Timur to Selatan fibre cut"/>
<check id="c3" kind="outage" from="pc0" to="server0" url="utara:GigabitEthernet0/1" expect="ok" label="WargaSelatan still reaches LayananKota with the Utara to Timur fibre cut"/>
</takumi>
